/*
 * White Whale :: klone run-only config for FALLET2022_MICROBIAL_TRANSGEN_WGBS
 *
 * Passed last, after the study config (docs/compute_profiles.md):
 *
 *   nextflow run workflows/methylation -c config/FALLET2022_MICROBIAL_TRANSGEN_WGBS.config \
 *       -c data/studies/FALLET2022_MICROBIAL_TRANSGEN_WGBS/klone.run.config -profile klone
 *
 * It lives under data/studies/ because a study PR may only touch that folder
 * and config/<STUDY_ID>.config (whale check-study-scope).
 *
 * Why: 47 libraries of 67-161 M pairs at 2 x 150 bp, 1735 Gb of sequence.
 * DECICOMP2025's Bismark alignments on klone (its trace, 2026-11-18..23) ran
 * at a median 28.3 M pairs/h per 16-CPU task on coenv compute and 42.1 on
 * srlab cpu-g2-mem2x. At the slower rate these libraries take an estimated
 * 2.4-5.8 h (median 4.4 h), so nearly none fits the ckpt-all window
 * (4 h 30 m) and BISMARK_ALIGN runs entirely on the lab's non-preemptible
 * partitions, alternating between coenv compute and srlab cpu-g2-mem2x by a
 * stable hash of the sample id. coenv cpu-g2 is not used, which holds the
 * project's 32-CPU / 200 GB convention for that partition
 * (docs/compute_profiles.md). Slurm caps each lane at the lab's share, so two
 * run on each and the rest wait in the queue. The hash puts 24 libraries
 * (918 Gb) on compute and 23 (818 Gb) on cpu-g2-mem2x, so alignment takes an
 * estimated 2.3 days, set by the compute lane.
 *
 * Everything else (FastQC, trimming, deduplication, extraction, summaries)
 * stays on ckpt-all as the profile has it.
 */

process {
    withName: 'BISMARK_ALIGN' {
        // Bismark's temporary FASTQ goes to the node's /scr, not the shared
        // (and often full) /gscratch.
        scratch        = '/scr'
        maxForks       = 8
        cpus           = 16
        time           = '24h'
        // coenv compute is 40 CPUs / 188 GB, shared with two 8 GB head jobs
        // (this study's and GAWRA2023's), so 80 GB lets two aligners run
        // there. DECICOMP's peak RSS at 160 M pairs was 22.9 GB.
        memory         = { Math.floorMod(sample_id.hashCode(), 2) == 0 ? '80 GB' : '240 GB' }
        queue          = { Math.floorMod(sample_id.hashCode(), 2) == 0 ? 'compute' : 'cpu-g2-mem2x' }
        clusterOptions = { Math.floorMod(sample_id.hashCode(), 2) == 0 ? '--account=coenv' : '--account=srlab' }
    }
}
